w","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each element stands in a tower of levels, one more with probability 1\/4, so a search skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ahead on the upper levels and finishes on the bottom one. Lookup, insertion and removal take"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") expected time, with no rebalancing. Every link also records how many elements it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes, so the elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like an array: "},{"code":"list[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index costs O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var numbers: SkipList = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","numbers.insert(4)","Array(numbers)                \/\/ [1, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9]","numbers.lowerBound(5)         \/\/ 3, the index of 5","numbers[1]                    \/\/ 3"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tower heights come from a random number generator given at creation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator"},{"type":"text","text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The list draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heights as its 